{
  "assessment": "The source provides a quantitative test of Kramers-Langer theory for thermally activated inversion of a five-ion pyramidal Coulomb cluster. The identical-ion (40Ca+) cluster exhibits a low-barrier pseudo-rotation pathway with measured inversion rates spanning two orders of magnitude, fitted to the K-L formula to yield a temperature of 1.8±0.1 mK. The isotope-substituted (44Ca+ at apex) cluster shows suppression of thermal activation via a high-barrier turnstile rotation. The source reports activation barriers for both pathways (pseudo-rotation ~20 mK, turnstile ~270 mK) and a background collision rate R_bg = 0.10±0.03 s^-1. The control is the trap aspect ratio alpha, with a bistable range 1.05<alpha<1.29 for identical ions and a threshold alpha_th ~1.1. The readout is the inversion rate kappa. The source provides sufficient quantitative detail for a case with two regimes (identical vs isotope-substituted) sharing the alpha control, though the isotope-substituted regime lacks a measured rate formula. The K-L formula is given with parameters (prefactor, barrier, Hessian determinants) that can be used as a mechanism. The source is deemed case_authoring_ready.",
  "case_authoring_ready": true,
  "source": {
    "citation": "Akhil Ayyadevara, Symmetry-Controlled Thermal Activation in Pyramidal Coulomb Clusters: Testing Kramers-Langer Theory, Physical Review Letters (2026), DOI:10.1103/xsdn-srjd",
    "journal_doi": "10.1103/xsdn-srjd",
    "arxiv_versioned_id": "2601.04883v1"
  },
  "paper_scope": "The paper studies thermally activated inversion dynamics of a five-ion pyramidal Coulomb cluster in a Paul trap. It compares identical-ion (40Ca+) clusters, which invert via a low-barrier pseudo-rotation, with isotope-substituted (44Ca+ apex) clusters, which invert via a high-barrier turnstile rotation. The central quantitative result is a parameter-free test of multidimensional Kramers-Langer theory against measured inversion rates, yielding a cluster temperature of 1.8±0.1 mK. The paper also reports activation barriers for the two pathways and a background collision rate.",
  "mechanisms": [
    {
      "mechanism_id": "kramers_langer_rate",
      "statement": "The escape rate from a local minimum in a multidimensional energy landscape is given by the Kramers-Langer formula: kappa = N * (lambda^+ / 2pi) * sqrt(det U / |det U'|) * exp(-E_b / k_B T), where E_b is the energy barrier, U and U' are Hessians at equilibrium and saddle, lambda^+ is the positive eigenvalue of the dynamical matrix at the saddle, and N is the number of equivalent pathways.",
      "equations": [
        "kappa = N * (lambda^+ / (2*pi)) * sqrt(det(U) / |det(U')|) * exp(-E_b / (k_B * T))",
        "det(m * lambda^2 * I + gamma * lambda * I + U') = 0"
      ],
      "variable_names": [
        "kappa",
        "N",
        "lambda^+",
        "U",
        "U'",
        "E_b",
        "k_B",
        "T",
        "gamma"
      ],
      "parameters": [
        {
          "name": "N_identical",
          "value": 4,
          "uncertainty": "none",
          "unit": "dimensionless",
          "role": "Number of equivalent pathways for identical-ion cluster",
          "anchors": [
            {
              "line_start": 147,
              "line_end": 147,
              "support": "We also set N = 4 since the apex ion can replace any of the four base ions."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "E_b_pseudo_rotation",
          "value": 0.02,
          "uncertainty": "none",
          "unit": "K",
          "role": "Activation barrier for pseudo-rotation pathway in identical-ion cluster",
          "anchors": [
            {
              "line_start": 448,
              "line_end": 448,
              "support": "This path relaxes to the Berry pseudo-rotation MEP, avoiding the high-energy center and reducing the activation barrier by two orders of magnitude (from ~1 K to ~20 mK)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "E_b_turnstile_rotation",
          "value": 0.27,
          "uncertainty": "none",
          "unit": "K",
          "role": "Activation barrier for turnstile rotation pathway in isotope-substituted cluster",
          "anchors": [
            {
              "line_start": 450,
              "line_end": 450,
              "support": "The activation barrier is ~270 mK, which is significantly lower than the umbrella inversion but sufficiently high to suppress thermal activation at experimental temperatures."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "anchors": [
        {
          "line_start": 137,
          "line_end": 145,
          "support": "The escape rate from a local minimum predicted by the multidimensional K-L theory is kappa = N (lambda^+/2pi) (det U / |det U'|)^{1/2} exp(-E_b/k_B T), where E_b is the energy barrier and U, U' are Hessians at equilibrium and saddle. The prefactor lambda^+ is the single positive eigenvalue of the dynamical matrix at the saddle, det(m lambda^2 I + gamma lambda I + U') = 0. N denotes the number of equivalent pathways."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "fixed_conditions": [
    {
